# Folio Project Rules

## Stack
- PHP 8.3, SQLite, no framework
- Docker Compose for local development
- Built-in PHP dev server (no Apache/Nginx)

## Conventions
- Functions live in `lib/bootstrap.php` (helpers) or `lib/migrate.php` (migration runner)
- Pages are standalone PHP files in `public/`
- All user-facing strings must be escaped with `h()` (wrapper for htmlspecialchars)
- Database access via the `db()` singleton (PDO with exceptions enabled)
- Schema changes MUST go through numbered migration files in `migrations/` — never edit `schema.sql`

## Patterns to Follow
- Audit all state-changing actions: `audit_log($action, $entity_type, $entity_id, $details)`
- Use prepared statements for ALL queries (no string interpolation in SQL)
- POST/redirect/GET for form submissions
- Keep pages self-contained: each public/*.php handles its own routing, validation, and rendering

## Testing
- Tests live in `tests/test.php`, use the `test(name, fn)` / `assert_true()` pattern
- Tests re-seed the database before running (always start from known state)
- Run via: `docker compose exec app php tests/test.php`

## Migration Rules
- File naming: `NNN_description.php` (e.g., `001_add_publish_at_to_documents.php`)
- Each migration returns a closure: `return function (PDO $pdo): void { ... };`
- Migrations run in numeric order, tracked in `_migrations` table
- Must be idempotent when combined with the tracking table (won't re-run)

## Style
- 4-space indentation in PHP
- Single quotes for strings unless interpolation needed
- Type hints on function signatures
- No closing `?>` tag in pure-PHP files (prevents accidental whitespace)
